{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Problem\n\nAfter bug `nickelic-lazuline-gonolek` (Gerrit 3351), the tickets store no longer runs `git gc` on any path:\n- Every bounded git child runs with `maintenance.auto=false` and `gc.auto=0`.\n- The explicit write-locked step runs only `commit-graph`, `loose-objects` and `incremental-repack`.\n\nThat was deliberate. On the 1.07M-object production clone, `gc --auto` took 133.9 s and a full repack took 605.6 s, both past the step's 120 s bound. But it has two consequences:\n- Nothing ever prunes unreachable objects, such as the leftovers of failed writes, abandoned merges and compaction.\n- Nothing ever expires reflogs. The production `.git/logs/HEAD` was 4.5 MB on 2026-11-11.\n\nGrowth is slow (see Measurements; an earlier loose-only count of about 1,800 objects is superseded). Even so, the growth is unbounded.\n\nTwo docs still describe the old posture:\n- `docs/concurrency.md`, in the caveat paragraph: \"keeps auto-gc ENABLED\" and \"It reclaims loose/pack growth on its own\".\n- `docs/scale-envelope.md`: stock `git gc` runs in the foreground of the write command and handles packing.\n\n## Decision (recorded 2026-11-12, coordinator; option (1) of the 2026-11-11 Decision comment)\n\n- Reflog entries: expired inside the existing write-locked maintenance step, using git's own expiry defaults (`gc.reflogExpire` 90 days, `gc.reflogExpireUnreachable` 30 days). No config key, env var or flag.\n- Unreachable objects: growth is ACCEPTED at its measured rate, with an operator-run reclaim documented in a runbook.\n\n## Measurements (production tickets clone, read-only, via SSM)\n\nUnreachable objects, counted across loose AND packed storage (2026-11-12 ~02:05 PST):\n- Total objects: 1,071,252 in packs (35 packs) + 95 loose = 1,071,347. Packs can hold duplicate copies, so this total is an upper bound.\n- Reachable objects: `git rev-list --objects --all | wc -l` = 1,071,190, and the same 1,071,190 with `--reflog` added. So reflogs keep no extra objects alive today.\n- Unreachable objects are therefore at most 157 (about 0.015%), accumulated since the clone was made on 2026-08-26 PDT: an upper bound of about 157 objects in 2.5 months. Each reachability walk took 107-112 s.\n- Earlier loose-only counts (1,800; 28) are not a growth measure: `loose-objects` packs unreachable loose objects too.\n\nReflog expiry cost: `git reflog expire --dry-run --all` took 0.01-0.06 s over 3 runs (3 refs, HEAD reflog 4.69 MB / 25,933 entries).\n\nGit version: maintenance's `reflog-expire` task needs git 2.50; the production MCP container runs 2.47.3 (measured 2026-11-12), where an unknown task fails the whole `maintenance run`. So the step calls `git reflog expire --all` directly.\n\n## Approach\n\n1. `src/rebar/_store/event_commit_git.py::run_auto_maintenance`, still under the caller's write lock:\n   - After `maintenance run`, run `git reflog expire --all` through `run_git_reaped` with its own fixed 30 s timeout (a module constant), so the worst-case lock hold is the maintenance bound plus 30 s.\n   - Skip it when maintenance could not launch (`None`) or timed out (124), so a slow step never adds more.\n   - Any failure (non-zero exit including 128, or OSError) is logged as a warning and never raised. A 124 is logged as an ERROR that lists every `*.lock` under the common git dir's top level, `refs/` and `logs/`: rebar reclaims only index.lock, so a ref lock stranded by the kill blocks writes until removed. Measured cost of a real (non-dry) expiry on a 26,000-entry reflog: 0.02-0.03 s.\n   - The return value is unchanged (the maintenance result).\n2. `infra/runbooks/tickets-store-prune.md` (new), the operator-run reclaim:\n   - Measure first: unreachable upper bound = (in-pack + count) - `git rev-list --objects --all --reflog | wc -l`. Reclaim only when material.\n   - Reclaim with `git -c pack.threads=1 gc --cruft --prune=2.weeks.ago` (git's own tool; a cruft repack alone leaves expired LOOSE objects, gc also prunes them). Verified locally on git 2.56: a 30-day-old unreachable loose object and packed object were both removed, a fresh one kept. Full repack, 605.6 s measured (bug nickelic-lazuline-gonolek).\n   - Run inside the live MCP container under `rebar._store.lock.write_lock`; writes in that window fail with a lock timeout, so use a quiet window. Verify by re-measuring; no rollback needed.\n3. `docs/concurrency.md` caveat and `docs/scale-envelope.md` §\"Git maintenance & gc\" describe the current posture:\n   - No implicit gc or maintenance.\n   - The explicit locked step runs commit-graph, loose-objects, incremental-repack, then reflog expiry.\n   - Unreachable objects are reclaimed only by the operator runbook (for any store shape; the runbook's commands are written for the production MCP deployment).\n   - This replaces \"keeps auto-gc ENABLED\", \"reclaims loose/pack growth on its own\" and \"Foreground auto-gc handles packing\".\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/_store/event_commit_git.py`\n- `src/rebar/_store/sync.py` (module docstring still described foreground auto-gc)\n- `tests/unit/test_store_reflog_expiry.py` (new)\n- `tests/unit/test_store_maintenance_gonolek.py` (its exact-calls test gains the reflog call)\n- `infra/runbooks/tickets-store-prune.md` (new)\n- `docs/concurrency.md`\n- `docs/scale-envelope.md`\n\n## Testing\n\n- RED then GREEN: a real git repo with isolated config has HEAD reflog entries dated (via `GIT_COMMITTER_DATE`) 120, 60, 45 (unreachable) and 1 day ago. After `run_auto_maintenance`, the 120-day and 45-day entries are gone and the 1-day entry remains. Fails on the pre-fix tree.\n- With `gc.reflogExpire=never` and `gc.reflogExpireUnreachable=never` set in the repo, every entry survives, proving the step passes no expiry value of its own.\n- Why the test does not assert git's 90/30-day split: see the 2026-11-12 implementation comment (measured on git 2.56).\n- Failure arms, with `run_git_reaped` faked: the reflog call raising OSError, returning 124, or returning 128 each logs a warning, raises nothing, and still returns the maintenance result.\n- When maintenance returns 124 or cannot launch, the reflog call is not made.\n- `test_explicit_step_runs_exactly_the_incremental_tasks` asserts the maintenance call followed by `reflog expire --all`.\n- Docs check before commit: `git grep -n` finds none of `keeps auto-gc`, `reclaims loose/pack growth on its own`, `Foreground auto-gc handles packing` (the first is matched alone because the original phrase wraps a line).\n- A 124 test plants `.git/HEAD.lock` and asserts the error names it.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Unreachable objects and reflog entries on the tickets store are reclaimed on some bounded cadence that never runs outside the write lock, or a recorded decision accepts unbounded growth with its measured rate.\n- [ ] Reflog entries past git's expiry policy are expired by the write-locked maintenance step, shown by a test that fails on the pre-fix tree, and the repository's own `gc.reflogExpire*` settings govern (no value is hard-coded), shown by a test.\n- [ ] A failing, erroring or timed-out reflog expiry is logged and never raised, and it is skipped after a timed-out maintenance run, shown by tests.\n- [ ] The recorded decision states the measured unreachable-object rate counted across packs, and `infra/runbooks/tickets-store-prune.md` documents a reclaim that removes packed unreachable objects under the write lock.\n- [ ] `docs/concurrency.md` and `docs/scale-envelope.md` describe the current maintenance posture and no longer contain the 3 stale phrases.\n- [ ] [non-codebase] `env -u JIRA_URL -u JIRA_USER -u JIRA_API_TOKEN make verify` exits 0 on the commit pushed for review.\n  provenance: environment=macOS dev host, fix-xiphias worktree; principal=Rebar Bot Nava; privilege_posture=narrower; instrument=live-call — exit status and log live outside the repository\n"}},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1794480537519029001,"uuid":"e574cdf7-e642-40e2-8555-22a5df9fe512"}